--- !u!114 &1290627256086133
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1910817642585643}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 396459964a4a45a4b7cef4c9082df875, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPC
  displayName: "Monsieur Firmin"
  title: "One of the Opera's new managers"
  tint: {r: 0.5, g: 0.4, b: 0.2, a: 1}
  lines:
  - text: "I am not in the mood to let myself be laughed at long,"
  - text: "Don't be afraid: you never had that reputation,"
  - text: "Oh, you agree, do you? You agree! It's a joke! And you think it funny, no doubt?"
  - text: "Good morning, M. Lachenel, To what do we owe the honor of your visit?"
  - text: "Well, who could have thought it? But don't be afraid ... next time, I shall have taken my precautions."
  - text: "Ah, we are delighted ... Look here, Mme. Giry, We may just as well tell you, among ourselves ... you're no fool!"
  - text: "Aha! I knew nothing either! You put twenty-thousand francs in my pocket and I knew nothing either! I am very glad to hear it, Mme. Giry!"
  - text: "Of course! It's very clever of O. G."
  - text: "But, in that case, they will never steal our twenty-thousand francs!"
  - text: "It's incredible! I am sure of my servants ... and if one of them had done it, he would have disappeared since."
  - text: "The ghost! The ghost! Suppose, all the same, it were a ghost who puts the magic envelopes on the table ... who talks in Box Five ... who killed Joseph Buquet ..."
  - text: "Never mind, go on, go on!"
